<TSL-SYSTEM Tools> %Network@network, A module which probes and analyses the network.

Usage: COMMAND [ARGUMENTS]

Commands:
    help / @help            Print this HelpPage.
    list                    List the available commands.
    dns HOST [TYPE]         Resolve DNS records. TYPE can be A, AAAA, CNAME, MX, NS, TXT, SOA or PTR.
    ping HOST [COUNT]       Send ICMP echo requests and report the round-trip time.
    port HOST [PORTS]       Scan TCP ports. PORTS accepts 'top', '80,443' or '1-1024'.
    trace HOST [HOPS]       Trace the route to a host and show every hop.
    http URL                Analyze an HTTP/HTTPS response: status, headers, timing and security headers.
    tls HOST [PORT]         Inspect the TLS certificate and the negotiated cipher.
    whois TARGET            Query the whois record of a domain or an IP address.
    local                   Show the local interfaces, gateway, DNS servers and ARP table.
    public                  Show the public IP address and its location.
    speed [URL]             Measure the download speed and the TCP handshake latency.
    analyze TARGET          Run all of the checks above against one target.
    @exit                   Return to the ExecuteShell or the Terminal.
    @flush                  Flush the module cache.

Examples:
    dns example.com
    dns example.com MX
    ping github.com 6
    port 127.0.0.1 22,80,443
    trace example.com
    http https://example.com
    tls github.com 443
    whois example.com
    speed
    analyze https://example.com

Notes:
    Port scanning and whois queries should only be used against hosts you own
    or are authorized to test. The module never sends exploit payloads; it only
    performs ordinary DNS, ICMP, TCP and HTTP requests.

